From: sneid1 <sneid1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:01:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] UYA: warp to any level through the game's own level
 change (rc3/warp.rs)

Between fields the host calls the current level's request_level_change(level, 0) (rac3-decomp func_0038E5B8, one copy per
single-player level program, its first words checked), with the registers saved and restored and interrupts masked. The level's
main loop then runs level_change, level_switch and level_load with the level's own transition and set-up. A level the story state
maps to another (Holostar 13 -> 23) is set back to the one asked for, and reported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oracle/src/rc3/mod.rs  |  1 +
 oracle/src/rc3/warp.rs | 74 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 75 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 oracle/src/rc3/warp.rs

diff --git a/oracle/src/rc3/mod.rs b/oracle/src/rc3/mod.rs
